## Resource Requirements

| Run | Duration | Notes |
|-----|----------|-------|
| `scripts/run_smoke_test.sh` | [TO COMPLETE: re-measure on the test machine below, after the release rebuild] | 10 programs, the two comparisons |
| `scripts/run_full_evaluation.sh --subset` | about 3 h on the paper's machine (estimate) | 100 programs of `benchmarks/subset`, each Ultimate run capped at 300 s; see *Subset version* |
| `scripts/run_full_evaluation.sh` | about 11 days on the paper's machine (estimate) | 3,430 programs, the paper's timeouts; the script prints the worst case at start-up |

Ultimate is the expensive part: ULR vs P-ULR runs it once per program and ULR vs UPL twice, each
run capped by its timeout: 3,000 s to extract the lasso traces of ULR vs P-ULR, and 1,000 s per run
of ULR vs UPL, the values the paper used and the scripts' defaults. PaSTTeL is comparatively cheap:
on the 11,282 lasso traces of the paper's ULR vs P-ULR run, the P-ULR-Seq pass took about 20
minutes and the P-ULR-Par7 pass about 17.

Both estimates come from the paper's logs. Extracting the lasso traces took 88 h for the 2,860
programs of the paper's run, about 110 s per program including PaSTTeL. ULR vs UPL took about 160 s
per program over the 220 programs measured so far. For the full evaluation, this gives
3,430 x (110 + 160) s, about 11 days.
[TO COMPLETE: re-estimate from the ULR vs UPL run of the rebuilt release]

The paper's results were produced on:
- Ubuntu 24.04, x86-64, 16 vCPUs (virtual machine, host processor not exposed), 29 GB RAM
- Z3 4.16.0
- timeouts: Ultimate 3,000 s per program to extract lasso traces and 1,000 s per program and per
  run for ULR vs UPL; PaSTTeL 600 s per lasso trace in ULR vs P-ULR and
  20 s per lasso inside UPL. These are the scripts' defaults (`scripts/common.sh`).

The artifact was tested on:
- Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS, x86-64
- AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 6850H (8 cores, 16 threads), 30 GB RAM
- Java 21, Z3 4.16.0, CVC5 1.3.4 (installed, not used by the experiments)

